cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Automated EEG Analysis (AEA)"
message: >
  Cite AEA and record the software version or commit used. Also cite the source
  papers declared by the recipes you use. The referenced Zenodo dataset preserves
  resources and validation records frozen on 6 November 2026 and is separate
  from the current software packages.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hou
    given-names: Dengzhe
    affiliation: Tohoku University
repository-code: "https://github.com/dengzhe-hou/auto-eeg-analysis"
url: "https://dengzhe-hou.github.io/auto-eeg-analysis/"
abstract: >
  AEA is an open library of EEG analysis skills for MNE-Python, with executable
  specifications and a numerically certified core. It provides shareable
  paradigm-specific recipes, automatic COBIDAS-MEEG methods-text generation,
  and a pre-submission reviewer-anticipation audit. EEGLAB and FieldTrip provide
  independent validation and selected alternative backend paths.
keywords:
  - EEG
  - electroencephalography
  - reproducibility
  - LLM agent
  - Claude Code
  - automated analysis
  - MNE-Python
  - EEGLAB
  - FieldTrip
license: MIT
references:
  - type: data
    title: "Reusable skills for electroencephalography analysis with large language model agents (resources and validation records)"
    authors:
      - family-names: Hou
        given-names: Dengzhe
        affiliation: Tohoku University
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24012489"
    url: "https://zenodo.org/records/24012489"
    version: "2026-11-06"
    date-released: 2026-11-07
